    "q-166805": {
      "dom_id": "question-166805",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "To prepare liquid fertilizer, $5.5$ grams of fertilizer powder should be dissolved in a liter of water. How much powder must be dissolved in $8.6$ liters of water to make fertilizer?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Expressed as a decimal, \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$grams of powder must be dissolved in $8.6$ liters of water.",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the amount of powder that must be dissolved in $8.6$ liters of water, we have to multiply $8.6$ by $5.5.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{3} \\\\ \\boxed{3}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $8.6$ and there is $1$ decimal place in $5.5.$\nTherefore, their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $4730$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n47\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{30}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nHence, $8.6\\times 5.5=47.30=47.3.$\n\nWe conclude that $47.3$ grams of powder must be dissolved in $8.6$ liters of water.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
